WEBVTT

00:17.800 --> 00:22.182
The final spotlight fades across the empty

00:22.342 --> 00:27.644
arena floor The road cases are latched and

00:27.744 --> 00:33.767
rolled outside the stage door For twenty years

00:33.847 --> 00:40.269
we gave the world the thunder in our chest Now the

00:40.369 --> 00:46.172
highway's calling us to finally take our rest

00:47.169 --> 00:52.293
Our custom low floor shuttle bus Is kneeling at

00:52.333 --> 00:59.079
the curb Leading to a quiet place The static

00:59.239 --> 01:05.345
can't disturb Aluminum ramp unfolds beneath

01:05.425 --> 01:12.030
the amber sign Five of us together At the end of

01:12.050 --> 01:12.591
the line

01:15.488 --> 01:20.771
We're taking the last bus home Back to Progress

01:20.831 --> 01:26.353
Street Turning off the amplifiers And the

01:26.454 --> 01:32.556
stadium heat Lock the front door tight and let

01:32.616 --> 01:36.018
the curtains fall We don't owe the outside world

01:36.098 --> 01:38.840
anything at all Through every storm we

01:38.900 --> 01:42.322
weathered and every song we played This family

01:42.382 --> 01:48.546
is the greatest music that we ever made

01:52.809 --> 01:57.292
Unplug the synthesizers, set the guitars in

01:57.312 --> 02:03.001
their stands Rest the tired voices and the

02:03.061 --> 02:09.102
calloused aching hands Five pairs of sneakers

02:09.542 --> 02:13.943
lined up by the wooden stairs Trade in all the

02:14.003 --> 02:19.224
crowded rooms for quiet living room chairs

02:20.484 --> 02:25.453
We're not fading into nothing We're just tuning

02:25.633 --> 02:29.816
out the noise Back to three sisters and brothers

02:30.416 --> 02:36.040
And the twin ride boys We're taking the last bus

02:36.100 --> 02:42.644
home Back to Progress Street Turning off the

02:42.664 --> 02:49.837
amplifiers And the stadium heat Lock the front

02:49.937 --> 02:52.660
door tight and let the curtains fall We don't

02:52.840 --> 02:56.384
know the outside world, anything at all Through

02:56.504 --> 02:59.227
every storm we weathered and every song we

02:59.267 --> 03:03.091
played This family is the greatest music that we

03:03.211 --> 03:03.712
ever made

03:18.141 --> 03:22.402
Someday when we're ready We'll turn the

03:22.422 --> 03:28.883
switches on And find out that the fire In the

03:29.023 --> 03:32.784
engine's never gone But tonight the porch

03:33.024 --> 03:40.045
light's turning off In Blacksburg town As we lay

03:40.105 --> 03:47.527
the heavy burden Of the road right down

04:13.321 --> 04:19.242
We're taking the last bus home Back to Progress

04:19.282 --> 04:23.942
Street Turning off the amplifiers And the

04:23.962 --> 04:30.784
stadium heat Lock the front door tight and let

04:30.844 --> 04:34.125
the curtains fall We don't owe the outside world

04:34.285 --> 04:37.346
anything at all Through every storm we weather

04:37.386 --> 04:40.687
and every song we play This family is the

04:40.727 --> 04:45.168
greatest music That we ever made

04:49.872 --> 04:55.768
Lights out on Progress Street Good night, Forge

04:55.788 --> 04:56.851
Nation

